CREATED:20260509T210539Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260509T210539Z
UID:120781-1779897600-1779901200@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Virtual Naturalist: Sea Turtles
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever been lucky enough to see a sea turtle in the wild? These beautiful reptiles have some amazing adaptations that allow them to live in salt water.  Join us for a virtual program perfect for ages 8+ to learn about how they survive in the ocean\, and what you can do to help protect them. \n\n\n\n\nRegister
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/virtual-naturalist-sea-turtles/
LOCATION:Virtual\, NC\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Children,Citizen Science,K-12 Students,Teens,Virtual
ORGANIZER;CN="Jennifer%20Tredway":MAILTO:jennifer.tredway@naturalsciences.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Museum of Natural Sciences
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T120000
DTSTAMP:20260524T003520
CREATED:20260509T191614Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260509T191614Z
UID:120753-1779962400-1779969600@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Great Sunflower Project
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators are beautiful\, fascinating\, and crucial members of Piedmont ecosystems\, and spring is a wonderful time to observe and learn from them! As global change threatens insect populations worldwide\, it is more important than ever that we monitor these important species. Come be a part of this effort\, as we learn about the pollinators that live at Prairie Ridge\, look for them around the Ecostation\, and contribute observations to The Great Sunflower Project\, a collaborative science project supporting active pollinator research\, education\, and conservation. Come dressed for the weather and ready for about a half-mile walk for this program for ages 8+. \nRegistration is required to attend this program. \nRegister
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/great-sunflower-project-2-2/
LOCATION:Prairie Ridge\, 1671 Gold Star Drive\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Children,Citizen Science,Educators,K-12 Students,Outdoor Experiences,Teens
ORGANIZER;CN="Julie%20Hall":MAILTO:julie.hall@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.812182885871;-78.713963528554
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Prairie Ridge 1671 Gold Star Drive Raleigh NC 27607 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=1671 Gold Star Drive:geo:-78.713963528554,35.812182885871
END:VEVENT
