SUMMARY:Lifelong Hike: Picture Creek
DESCRIPTION:We will hike through the world’s largest population of the federally endangered smooth coneflower in peak bloom during this visit to the Picture Creek nature preserve.  This power line corridor through a unique diabase geologic area gives us a good sense of what the piedmont prairies were like in earlier times. You will see wildflowers here that you don’t see in most areas of the piedmont. \nPlease note: You will be required to enter the following information for each registrant before you can complete your registration: emergency contact\, physician contact and health information (allergies\, conditions\, medications relevant to this field experience). Take a moment to gather this information before beginning your registration. \nREGISTRATION FOR THIS TRIP IS FULL \nIf the trip is full\, please email Missy Chernick to be added to the waitlist. \nRegistration deadline: Monday\, June 1 at 7:00 AM \nFor additional information about this trip and other Lifelong Hikes & Adventures\, contact Jerry Reynolds at 919.707.9884.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/lifelong-hike-picture-creek-5/
LOCATION:In the Field
CATEGORIES:Adults,Lifelong Learners,Outdoor Experiences,Trips
END:VEVENT
